  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Byzacena coast LBY/TUN. Mattingly (1995) explains that <em>Libyphoenices</em> was the Greek and Roman name for the non-tribal town-dwelling agriculturalists who succeeded the Phoenicians of the Libyan coast.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A numerous, loosely affiliated people of the Byzacium and Tripolitana coasts",
